<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nukus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nukus is the capital of the Republic of Karakalpakstan in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a>. A small settlement until the Soviet period, it replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turtkul">Turtkul</a> as capital in 1939 and grew into an industrial city. It is known for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savitsky-museum">Savitsky Museum</a> of Soviet avant-garde art, and in 2022 it saw deadly protests against plans to end Karakalpakstan's right to secede.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nukus.jpg" alt="Nukus" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aziko9 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berdaq_at%C4%B1nda%C7%B5%C4%B1_Qaraqalpaq_%C3%A1debiyat%C4%B1_tariyx%C4%B1_m%C3%A1mleketlik_muzeyi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
